       "Decomposition reaction: a single reactant breaks down into two or more products, e.g. CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (on heating).",
       "Displacement reaction: a more reactive element displaces a less reactive one from its compound, e.g. Fe + CuSO₄ → FeSO₄ + Cu.",
       "Double displacement reaction: exchange of ions between two compounds, e.g. Na₂SO₄ + BaCl₂ → BaSO₄ (white precipitate) + 2NaCl.",
