       "Ionic compounds form by transfer of electrons (NaCl, MgO) — they have high melting/boiling points, conduct electricity in molten or aqueous state, and are brittle.",
       "Preventing corrosion: painting, oiling/greasing, galvanisation (zinc coating), alloying, chrome plating, anodising (aluminium).",
       "An alloy is a homogeneous mixture of metals; amalgam contains Hg; brass = Cu+Zn, bronze = Cu+Sn, solder = Pb+Sn.",
       "22-carat gold suits jewellery (22/24 pure); 24-carat pure gold is too soft.",
       "Calcination: heating carbonate ores in absence of air; roasting: heating sulphide ores in excess air.",
       "Thermite reaction: Fe₂O₃ + 2Al → 2Fe + Al₂O₃ + heat — used for welding railway tracks.",
       "Properties of non-metals: dull, brittle, poor conductors of electricity (graphite exception), non-sonorous.",
       "Non-metal oxides are acidic — CO₂, SO₂ react with water to form acids.",
       "Non-metals do not displace hydrogen from acids; diamond is the hardest natural substance.",
       "Graphite is a good conductor of electricity and a lubricant — due to its layered structure.",
       "Electrolytic refining of copper: impure copper as anode, pure copper as cathode, CuSO₄ solution as electrolyte.",
       "A metal higher in the reactivity series displaces a lower metal from its salt solution — e.g. Fe dipped in CuSO₄ displaces Cu.",
       "Black coating (Ag₂S) on silver and green coating (basic copper carbonate) on copper are also examples of corrosion."
