      "points": [
       "Plant hormones: auxin (phototropism), gibberellins (stem growth), cytokinins (cell division) and abscisic acid (growth inhibitor).",
       "Tropism: directional movement — positive phototropism of shoots and positive geotropism of roots.",
       "Parts of the human brain: cerebrum (thinking-memory), cerebellum (balance-coordination) and medulla (breathing, heartbeat, BP — involuntary actions).",
       "Reflex action is a quick involuntary action controlled by the spinal cord; reflex arc: receptor → sensory neuron → spinal cord → motor neuron → muscle.",
       "Human hormones: insulin (pancreas — diabetes), thyroxine (thyroid — needs iodine), growth hormone (pituitary), adrenaline (emergency).",
       "In the nervous system, information travels as electrical impulses; at the neuromuscular junction it passes by chemical signals.",
       "Coordination: control by the nervous system (quick response in animals) and hormones (slow, long-term in plants and animals).",
       "Neuron: dendrite → cell body → axon; chemical signals pass at the synapse between two neurons.",
       "Reflex action: quick response by the spinal cord — e.g. pulling the hand away on touching a hot object.",
       "Reflex arc: receptor → sensory neuron → spinal cord → motor neuron → muscle — the brain is bypassed, saving time.",
       "Parts of the brain: cerebrum (thinking, memory, voluntary actions), cerebellum (balance, coordination of movements), medulla (heartbeat, breathing, blood pressure).",
       "The spinal cord is the centre of reflex actions and the pathway of messages between brain and body.",
       "Movements in plants: thigmotropism (touch-me-not), phototropism (shoot towards light), geotropism (root downward), hydrotropism, chemotropism.",
       "Tropism is growth-based directional movement; nasties are immediate movements independent of growth.",
       "Plant hormones: auxin (phototropism, cell elongation), gibberellin (stem growth), cytokinin (cell division), abscisic acid (growth inhibitor, closes stomata).",
       "Animal hormones are secreted by endocrine glands and reach target organs through blood.",
       "The pituitary is the master gland — it makes growth hormone; deficiency causes dwarfism, excess causes gigantism.",
       "Thyroid: thyroxine (needs iodine) — controls metabolism; deficiency causes goitre.",
       "Pancreas: insulin — controls blood sugar; deficiency causes diabetes.",
       "Adrenal: adrenaline — the emergency hormone ('fight or flight'), increases heartbeat.",
       "Testes: testosterone; ovaries: oestrogen — develop secondary sexual characters.",
       "A nerve impulse is an electrochemical signal; movement in muscle cells happens by change in arrangement of special proteins.",
       "Touch-me-not leaves droop by movement of water in cells on touching — an example of thigmonasty.",
       "Diabetic patients are given insulin externally; iodised salt prevents goitre.",
       "Besides the pituitary, the thyroid, adrenal, pancreas and testes/ovaries are major endocrine glands."
      ],
