       "In an arithmetic progression (AP), each term is obtained by adding a fixed number d (common difference) to the previous term.",
       "nth term: aₙ = a + (n-1)d, where a is the first term and d is the common difference.",
       "Sum of first n terms: Sₙ = n/2 [2a + (n-1)d] = n/2 (a + l), where l is the last term.",
       "If d > 0 the AP increases, if d < 0 it decreases, and if d = 0 all terms are equal.",
       "If a, b, c are in AP then 2b = a + c (b is the arithmetic mean).",
       "nth term from the end = l - (n-1)d, where l is the last term.",
       "Arithmetic Progression (AP): a, a+d, a+2d, ... — common difference d = a₂-a₁.",
