        "The three identities: (1) sin²θ + cos²θ = 1, (2) 1 + tan²θ = sec²θ, (3) 1 + cot²θ = cosec²θ. Proof of (1): sinθ = p/h, cosθ = b/h → sin²θ + cos²θ = (p²+b²)/h² = h²/h² = 1 (since p²+b² = h² by Pythagoras).",
